From 798f8740818090c943daa4d1e698a8cdc7e87221 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:33:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MFront: generic-parallel interface for behaviours and models

Integration of a behaviour, initialize functions, post-processings,
rotation functions and execution of the standalone models over a batch of
points, on CPUs or on GPUs, with the backends of the interface for
material properties (MFRONT_GPB_API_VERSION 4, same output status,
statistics and execution policies). The values of a point are copied in
local arrays and back with all the reads before the writes, the compiler
being unable to assume that the fields and the arrays don't overlap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
